# {{PROJECT_NAME}} agent context hub

This is an **agent-only** shared context hub for every coding agent working in this workspace.
The human operator does not read it directly. Agents translate internal IDs and evidence into
complete, unambiguous explanations in chat.

| Path | Ownership |
|---|---|
| `context/` | Stable workspace and repository facts, loaded on demand |
| `plans/` | Feature context, delivery state, evidence, and production readiness |
| `memories/` | Durable verified lessons |
| `docs/` | External document registry and project-owned adapters |
| `environments/` | Cross-environment capability and resource comparisons |
| `skills/` | Canonical project/workspace skills |
| `scripts/` | Project/workspace operational scripts |
| `_config/` | Secret-free hub and runtime declarations |
| `_tools/` | Portable deterministic tools governed by `letgo` |

## Invariants

- `letgo` owns the reusable frame and validation contract only.
- This hub is shared by every agent in the workspace.
- `config/`, `scripts/`, and `skills/` contain project/workspace-specific extensions.
- Agent-owned prose is concise English. Preserve external quotations and exact domain labels.
- An internal identifier is paired with its description outside its defining table.
- Git merge, environment deployment, runtime verification, and QC are separate facts.

